# WF-RV-01 — Removed Code Review File (Official)

## Purpose

`AI_DELETED_CODE_REVIEW.md` is a **temporary support file** for architectural review of the **current** review only.

It exists because the Cursor review UI no longer allows reliable selection/copy of deleted blocks.

It lets a reviewer (e.g. ChatGPT) compare:

- the proposed definitive file
- the deleted lines

It is **not** a deletion history, audit, diff, changelog, or patch.

**Invariant:** the file must **always** contain **exclusively** the files in the **current** review and their removed text. Files from previous reviews must not appear.

## Naming

- Primary: `AI_DELETED_CODE_REVIEW.md` (repo root)
- Accepted-set sidecar (gitignored): `AI_DELETED_CODE_REVIEW.accept`
- Alias (legacy): `AI_REMOVED_CODE_REVIEW.md` — prefer the primary name

## Rule 1 — One document

There is **exactly one** `AI_DELETED_CODE_REVIEW.md`. It accompanies the current review until conclusion.

## Rule 2 — Full regenerate every time (no append, no history)

Every generation **completely rewrites** the document.

- **NOT** incremental append
- **NOT** historical carry-over from previous reviews
- Contents = **only** files in the current review set
- **Current review set** = `--files=…` when provided (preferred after an activity), otherwise dirty paths minus accepted
- After an activity, the agent **MUST** pass `--files=` listing **only** the files touched in that activity (not the entire dirty working tree), unless the user explicitly asks to review all dirty files
- If the current review has 37 files, the document lists **only** those 37 (and only those with actual deletions)
- Target size: normally **under ~300–500 lines** even for large reviews (merge consecutive same-motivo blocks; omit files with no deletions; keep review batches scoped)

## Rule 3 — When files leave the document (acceptance closes review)

A file leaves the current review when it is **accepted**.

### What counts as acceptance

Any clear user confirmation that one or more files are accepted / approved closes their review, including (not limited to):

- explicit **ACCETTO** / «accetto» / «accettati» after ChatGPT (or other) review;
- confirmation that those files are accepted and no longer under review;
- equivalent wording that the review for those paths is done.

Accepted files are **no longer “in review”**.

### Mandatory automatic cleanup (no user reminder)

**Immediately** after acceptance, the agent **MUST** run:

```text
node scripts/_gen_deleted_code_review.js --accept=path/to/File.tsx
```

(or comma-separated / repeated `--accept=`).

This records the path in `AI_DELETED_CODE_REVIEW.accept` and **fully regenerates** the document without those files.

The user must **never** have to remember or request this cleanup manually.

Leaving accepted files in the document is a **workflow regression**.

## Rule 4 — Mandatory format (minimal)

For each file in the current review, report **only**:

```text
path/NomeFile.ext

Righe X-Y
<deleted text only>
Motivo:
<one line>
```

### Allowed

- File path (relative)
- `Righe X-Y` (also for a single line: `Righe X-X`)
- Raw deleted text
- `Motivo:` + exactly **one** reason line per block

### Forbidden

- `FILE`, `====` separators, `#` headings
- `Riga` (use `Righe` only)
- Code fences (`` ```ts ``, `` ```tsx ``, `` ```md ``, etc.)
- Long explanations, architectural comments
- Diff markers, new code, unchanged context
- Repeating the same Motivo on consecutive blocks — **merge** them into one block with one Motivo

### Motivo

- Maximum **one** line per block
- Why removed / which behavior it replaces
- Do **not** describe the new code
- Identical Motivo on consecutive blocks → single merged block

## Rule 5 — Ordering

1. Files sorted by relative path
2. Within a file, blocks in diff order (after consecutive Motivo merge)

## Rule 6 — Goal

Enable review of deleted lines **without** the Cursor diff viewer — current review only.

## Rule 7 — Current-review completeness

While a file is unaccepted and still in the current review set with deletions, its removed text **must** appear after regenerate.

## Rule 8 — Compatibility

Same naming and operating mode for acceptance. Generation policy is full regenerate (not append history).

## Rule 9 — Implementation scope

Update only WF-RV-01 workflow docs and the generator (`scripts/_gen_deleted_code_review.js`). Do not change application/runtime/services/DB/AI_CONTEXT/AI_CONTEXT_MASTER as part of WF-RV-01 maintenance.

## Rule 10 — Report operativo (mandatory when the archive changes)

Every time the agent modifies `AI_DELETED_CODE_REVIEW.md` (generation **or** cleanup), the final **Report operativo** **MUST** declare it explicitly.

The modified-files list **MUST** always include:

- `AI_DELETED_CODE_REVIEW.md`

with the reason:

- `aggiornato (nuove eliminazioni)` — after regenerate; **or**
- `pulito dopo accettazione file (workflow WF-RV-01)` — after `--accept`

**Never** omit this file from the report when it was modified.

## Agent operating procedure (mandatory)

### After any AI change set that touches files

1. Complete the code/doc edits.
2. **Fully regenerate** `AI_DELETED_CODE_REVIEW.md` for **this activity’s files only**:
   - `node scripts/_gen_deleted_code_review.js --files=a.tsx,b.ts,…`
   - List every path touched in the activity (comma-separated). Do **not** default to the entire dirty tree.
3. Declare `AI_DELETED_CODE_REVIEW.md` in the Report operativo (`aggiornato (nuove eliminazioni)`).
4. Never commit `AI_DELETED_CODE_REVIEW.md` / `.accept` (gitignored). Never ask the user to accept them as project source.

### When the user accepts one or more files

1. Treat those paths’ review as **closed**.
2. **Immediately** run `--accept=…` for all accepted paths (full regenerate without them).
3. Confirm the document no longer contains those files.
4. Declare `AI_DELETED_CODE_REVIEW.md` in the Report operativo (`pulito dopo accettazione file (workflow WF-RV-01)`).

## Generator CLI

```text
node scripts/_gen_deleted_code_review.js --files=a.tsx,b.ts
node scripts/_gen_deleted_code_review.js
node scripts/_gen_deleted_code_review.js --accept=src/path/File.tsx
node scripts/_gen_deleted_code_review.js --accept=a.tsx,b.ts
```

- `--files=…`: **full regenerate** for that activity’s paths only (required after an activity).
- Default (no `--files`): all dirty minus accepted — only if the review intentionally covers the whole dirty tree.
- `--accept=…`: mark accepted + full regenerate excluding them.

## Repository policy

`AI_DELETED_CODE_REVIEW.md` / `AI_DELETED_CODE_REVIEW.accept` / `AI_REMOVED_CODE_REVIEW.md`:

- MUST NEVER be committed
- MUST NEVER be merged as source of truth
- Discard after the overall review is complete

Official long-form copy: `AI_DEV_WORKFLOW/WORKFLOWS/WF_RV_01_DELETED_CODE_REVIEW.md`
